+    <!-- Swipe away to fully exit -->
+    <string name="swipe_away_force_stop_title">Swipe away to fully exit</string>
+    <string name="swipe_away_force_stop_summary">Force stop an app when its task is swiped from Recents, so it cannot restart itself in the background. Apps set to Unrestricted battery usage, apps running a foreground service, the current keyboard and launcher are never stopped.</string>
+    <string name="bg_force_stop_timeout_title">Auto-stop background apps</string>
+    <string name="bg_force_stop_mode_title">Cleanup method</string>
+    <string name="bg_trim_cached_procs_title">Also trim idle processes of unrestricted apps</string>
+    <string name="bg_trim_cached_procs_summary">Kill cached, idle processes even in apps set to Unrestricted battery usage. Useful for messaging apps whose mini-program or helper processes waste memory; the process holding the push connection is not affected.</string>
+    <!-- 自启动管理 -->
+    <string name="autostart_manager_title">Auto-start manager</string>
+    <string name="autostart_manager_summary">Choose which apps may start themselves when the device boots</string>
+    <string name="autostart_manager_footer">%1$d of %2$d apps may start themselves.
+
+Turning an app off cuts three paths it can use to start itself: the boot broadcast, a fake account authenticator (the system must bind it to enumerate accounts, which pins the app in memory), and a sync adapter (the sync framework wakes it on a timer, bypassing battery optimization). Measured here on one app store: 3 processes and 502 MB pinned as unreclaimable, down to 0 after a reboot.
+
+Only third-party apps are listed. System apps are not started by the boot broadcast, so this would have no effect on them.
+
+This cannot stop an app that another app calls into (sharing, payment callbacks). Messages and notifications may be delayed until you open the app.</string>
+    <string name="autostart_blocked_by_system">%1$s \u00b7 blocked by the system (the app re-enabled its own receiver)</string>
